WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.107
The applied challenge asks for the two longest completed stays in each department.

00:00:05.107 --> 00:00:09.462
Start by calculating the stay duration for each completed admission.

00:00:09.462 --> 00:00:13.082
The row grain is still one admission.

00:00:13.082 --> 00:00:17.407
Next, rank admissions within each department, with the longest stay first.

00:00:17.407 --> 00:00:22.767
Use admission I D as a stable tie-breaker when exact durations match.

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:27.037
Finally, keep the first two row numbers from each department.

00:00:27.037 --> 00:00:34.422
After the query runs, explain why the result still contains admission-level detail rather than one summary row per

00:00:34.422 --> 00:00:35.274
department.
